      ],
      "createdAt" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "description" : "In `milestoneNumbersIfNeeded`, the GitHub API query uses `per_page=100` but never follows the `Link` header for subsequent pages. Repositories with more than 100 milestones will silently have later ones excluded from the milestone name→number lookup. Any issue whose milestone falls in the unread pages will be synced without a milestone, with no warning to the user.\n",
      "environment" : "",
      "labels" : [

      ],
      "notes" : "GitHubSyncService.swift lines 163–165. GitHub paginates milestone lists; the full set requires following `Link: <url>; rel=\"next\"` until absent.",
      "number" : 4,
      "priority" : "medium",
      "relations" : [

      ],
      "remoteLinks" : [

      ],
      "reported" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "reportedBy" : "Code Review",
      "resolution" : "",
      "status" : "open",
      "stepsToReproduce" : [
        "Configure a GitHub repository that has more than 100 milestones.",
        "Assign one of the later milestones (position > 100) to a local issue.",
        "Sync to GitHub.",
        "Observe that the synced issue has no milestone set on GitHub."
      ],
      "title" : "Milestone lookup silently capped at 100 — no pagination",
      "type" : "bug",
      "updatedAt" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "uuid" : "C3D4E5F6-A7B8-9012-CDEF-012345678902"
    },
    {
      "area" : "IssueDetailView",
      "assignees" : [

      ],
      "comments" : [

      ],
      "createdAt" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "description" : "In `IssueDetailView`, both `relationsSection` and `remoteLinksSection` enumerate their arrays and use `id: \\.offset` as the SwiftUI list identity. Array position is not a stable identity: if items are reordered SwiftUI cannot track which view corresponds to which datum, causing incorrect animations and potentially stale view state. `Relation` has a stable `issueID`; `RemoteLink` has a stable `provider + identifier` pair. Both should be used instead of the offset.\n",
      "environment" : "",
      "labels" : [

      ],
      "notes" : "IssueDetailView.swift line 230 (relationsSection) and line 263 (remoteLinksSection). stepsToReproduce also uses offset (line 176) but plain strings have no natural ID, so offset is acceptable there.",
      "number" : 3,
      "priority" : "low",
      "relations" : [

      ],
      "remoteLinks" : [

      ],
      "reported" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "reportedBy" : "Code Review",
      "resolution" : "",
      "status" : "open",
      "stepsToReproduce" : [

      ],
      "title" : "Relations and remote links use array offset as SwiftUI identity",
      "type" : "bug",
      "updatedAt" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "uuid" : "B2C3D4E5-F6A7-8901-BCDE-F01234567891"
    },
    {
      "area" : "GitHubSyncView",
      "assignees" : [

      ],
      "comments" : [

      ],
      "createdAt" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "description" : "In `GitHubSyncView`, per-issue sync error strings are displayed with `ForEach(result.errors, id: \\.self)`. If two issues produce identical error messages (e.g., both return a 404), SwiftUI receives duplicate IDs in the same list, leading to undefined rendering behavior — typically one row silently disappearing.\n",
      "environment" : "",
      "labels" : [

      ],
      "notes" : "GitHubSyncView.swift line 93. Fix: use `.enumerated()` with `id: \\.offset`, or wrap errors in a small Identifiable struct.",
      "number" : 2,
      "priority" : "low",
      "relations" : [

      ],
      "remoteLinks" : [

      ],
      "reported" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "reportedBy" : "Code Review",
      "resolution" : "",
      "status" : "open",
      "stepsToReproduce" : [
        "Configure a valid GitHub repository.",
        "Add two local issues that will both fail to sync with the same error (e.g., label both with a milestone that doesn't exist and trigger a 422 with the same message).",
        "Sync.",
        "Observe the Last Sync error list — one row may be missing."
      ],
      "title" : "Sync error list misbehaves when two issues produce the same error message",
      "type" : "bug",
      "updatedAt" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "uuid" : "A1B2C3D4-E5F6-7890-ABCD-EF1234567890"
    },
    {
      "area" : "GitHubSyncService",
      "assignees" : [

      ],
      "comments" : [

      ],
      "createdAt" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "description" : "When a locally-resolved issue has no existing GitHub link, `sync()` calls `createIssue` (POST with `includeState: false` → created as open), then immediately calls `updateIssue` (PATCH with `state: \"closed\"`). GitHub's Issues API accepts `state` in POST requests. The create-then-close pattern fires a spurious \"closed\" event in the repository's activity feed, bumps the remote `updated_at` a second time, and uses an extra API call for every newly-synced resolved issue.\n",
      "environment" : "",
      "labels" : [

      ],
      "notes" : "GitHubSyncService.swift lines 64–68 and `payload(for:milestones:includeState:)` line 133–148. Fix: pass `includeState: true` to `createIssue` and remove the subsequent `updateIssue` call for the resolved-on-create path.",
      "number" : 5,
      "priority" : "low",
      "relations" : [

      ],
      "remoteLinks" : [

      ],
      "reported" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "reportedBy" : "Code Review",
      "resolution" : "",
      "status" : "open",
      "stepsToReproduce" : [
        "Create a local issue and mark it as resolved.",
        "Sync to GitHub for the first time.",
        "Check the repository's activity feed on GitHub.",
        "Observe two events: issue opened, then immediately closed."
      ],
      "title" : "Resolved issues create-then-close on first sync, producing spurious GitHub event",
      "type" : "bug",
      "updatedAt" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "uuid" : "E5F6A7B8-C9D0-1234-EF01-234567890124"
    },
    {
      "area" : "GitHubSyncService",
      "assignees" : [

      ],
      "comments" : [

      ],
      "createdAt" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "description" : "The sync service only pushes local issues to GitHub. Changes made directly on GitHub — comments, status updates, assignee edits, title changes — are never fetched back into the local document. A bi-directional sync would read each linked issue from `GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{number}` and merge remote changes (using `remoteUpdatedAt` for conflict detection).\n",
      "environment" : "",
      "labels" : [

      ],
      "notes" : "GitHubSyncService.swift sync() method. The RemoteLink already stores `remoteUpdatedAt` and `lastSyncedAt` for exactly this purpose — the pull side just hasn't been implemented.",
      "number" : 6,
      "priority" : "medium",
      "relations" : [

      ],
      "remoteLinks" : [

      ],
      "reported" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "reportedBy" : "Code Review",
      "resolution" : "",
      "status" : "open",
      "stepsToReproduce" : [

      ],
      "title" : "GitHub sync is push-only — remote changes are never pulled back",
      "type" : "feature",
      "updatedAt" : "2026-07-31T19:30:00Z",
      "uuid" : "D4E5F6A7-B8C9-0123-DEF0-123456789013"
    },
